  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Diocese of Homa Bay Integrated Food Security Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In this project CAFOD&#x2019;s partner Caritas Homa Bay aims to reduce community vulnerability to HIV and AIDS through the promotion of agro-enterprise and income diversification for 6000 households in Homa Bay county.  

According to the National AIDS Control Council survey report (2011) Homa Bay County&#x2019;s HIV and AIDS profile indicates prevalence of 27.1%, in comparison to a national prevalence of 5.6%.  As a result community members have experienced high child mortality rates; an increase in orphans and vulnerable children (OVCs) and child-headed households; an increase in the number of dependants per guardian; and reduced food production and access to food. 

Despite the high number of NGOs and government agencies intervening in the region, none of them are directly focusing on the food requirements of vulnerable groups. The communities do not have diversified sources of income and are instead confined to limited varieties of staple food crops of maize, beans and sorghum.

In response to these vulnerabilities Caritas Homa Bay plans to establish 60 Agro-Enterprise Development Groups (AEDGs) and 21 young farmer clubs, through which:
- crop diversification and small ruminants will be promoted and increased;
- resource mobilisation skills for the 6000 households through Savings and Internal Lending Communities (SILCs)  and a collective marketing approach will be enhanced.</narrative>
  </description>
